          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Yoneda lemma
            says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(c)
            into an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
            with the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(c)
            assigned by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the representing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p
            The Yoneda lemma is an elementary but deep and central result in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and in particular in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+and+topos+theory"} sheaf and topos theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+elements"} universal elements
          %h2#StatementOfYonedaLemma Statement and proof
          %h3#classical Classical
          #FunctorUnderlyingTheYonedaEmbedding.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                underlying the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C^{op}, Set] \coloneqq Func(C^{op}, Set)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              into
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              This is also called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(C^{op},Set))
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C &amp;\overset{y}{\longrightarrow}&amp; [C^op,Set]
                    \\\
                    c &amp;\mapsto&amp; Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(-,c)
                    }
            %p
              (called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              for reasons explained below) from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              to its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              into that object, also called the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} presheaf represented
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            %p
              The Yoneda embedding functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \to [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorUnderlyingTheYonedaEmbedding"}
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{C}^{op} \times \mathcal{C}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Set
            %p
              under the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(C^{op} \times C, Set)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Hom(C, [C^{op}, Set])
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              of categories.
          #YonedaLemma.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"}> Yoneda lemma
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              denoted
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},Set]
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorUnderlyingTheYonedaEmbedding"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{[C^op,Set]}(y(c),X) \;\simeq\; X(c)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(c)
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p
            This is the standard notation used mostly in pure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_c
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom(h_c, X) \simeq X(c)
          %p or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Nat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Nat(h_c, X) \simeq X(c)
          %p
            to emphasize that the morphisms of presheaves are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformations
            of the corresponding functors.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The proof is by chasing the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_c \in C(c, c)
              around both legs of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/naturality+square"} naturality square
              for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: C(-, c) \to X
              (hence a homomorphism of presheaves):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Id
                              %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Id
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo =
                              %mi def
                          %mtd
                            %mi ξ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi C
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi c
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C(c, c)
                    \&amp; \stackrel{\eta_c}{\to} &amp;
                    X(c) &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; Id_c &amp; \mapsto &amp; \eta_c(Id_c) &amp; \stackrel{def}{=} &amp; \xi \\
                    _\mathllap{C(f, c)} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow _\mathrlap{X(f)} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow _\mathrlap{X(f)} &amp; &amp; \\
                    C(b, c) &amp; \underset{\eta_b}{\to} &amp; X(b) &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; f &amp; \mapsto &amp; \eta_b(f) &amp; &amp;
                    }
            %p
              What this diagram shows is that the entire transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: C(-, c) \to X
              is completely determined from the single value
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \coloneqq \eta_c(Id_c) \in X(c)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_b: C(b, c) \to X(b)
              must take an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C(b, c)
              (i.e., a morphism
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: b \to c
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(f)(\xi)
            %p
              The crucial point is that the naturality condition on any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : C(-,c) \Rightarrow X
              is sufficient to ensure that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              is already entirely fixed by the value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c(Id_c) \in X(c)
              of its component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c : C(c,c) \to X(c)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_c
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            %p More in detail, the bijection is established by the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi c
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ev
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Id
                              %mi c
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C^{op}, Set](C(-,c),X)
                    \\stackrel{|_{c}}{\to}
                    Set(C(c,c), X(c))
                    \\stackrel{ev_{Id_c}}{\to}
                    X(c)
            %p
              where the first step is taking the component of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              and the second step is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_c \in C(c,c)
            %p
              The inverse of this map takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \in X(c)
              to the natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^\xi
              with components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi d
                      %mi ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta^\xi_d := X(-)(\xi) : C(d,c) \to X(d)
                    \\,.
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p
            Note: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
            calls a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+HoTT"} internal category in HoTT
            a “precategory” and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            a “category”, but here we shall refer to the standard terminology of “category” and “univalent category” respectively.
          %p
            By Lemma 9.5.3 in the HoTT book (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                      %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{y} : A \to \mathit{Set}^{A^{op}}
            which we call the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong yoneda embedding
          %p
            %strong Theorem 9.5.4 (The Yoneda Lemma)
            For any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                        %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathit{Set}^{A^{op}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                          %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi y
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi F
                  %mi a
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 9.5
                  %mn .5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_{\mathit{Set}^{A^{op}}}(\mathbf{y}a,F) \cong F a \qquad \qquad(9.5.5)
          %p
            Moreover this is natural in both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            %strong Proof.
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : \mathbf{y}a \to F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_a : \mathbf{y}a(a) \to F a
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{y} a(a)\equiv hom_A(a,a)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a:\mathbf{y}a(a)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_a(1_a):F a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \mapsto \alpha_a(1_a)
            from left to right in (9.5.5).
          %p
            In the other direction, given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: F a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi y
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : \mathbf{y} a \to F
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{a'}(f) \equiv F_{a,a'}(f)(x)
          %p Naturality is easy to check, so this gives a function from right to left in (9.5.5).
          %p
            To show that these are inverses, first suppose given
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: F a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            defined as above, we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi y
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : \mathbf{y}a \to F
            and define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            as above, then for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:hom_A(a',a)
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ,
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo ∘
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ,
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ,
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                              %mo ,
                              %mi a
                              %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
