            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+semicategory"} regular semicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma+for+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} Yoneda lemma for (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#References References
          %p
            For general references see any text on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "category+theory#References"} there
          %p
            The term
            %em Yoneda lemma
            originated in an interview of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nobuo+Yoneda"} Nobuo Yoneda
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"} Saunders Mac Lane
            at Paris Gare du Nord:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoshiki+Kinoshita"}> Yoshiki Kinoshita
                ,
                %em Nobuo Yoneda (1930-1996)
              %p &amp;
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Yoneda Lemma
              %p
                Math. Japonica,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 47
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/scans/yoneda.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MathJaponica_YonedaObituary.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mta.ca/~cat-dist/catlist/1999/yoneda"} posting to catlist in 1996
          %p
            In
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
            MacLane writes that this happened in 1954.
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/YonedaObituary.jpg"}/
          %p Review and exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/yoneda/yoneda.html"} Using Yoneda rather than J to present the identity type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                , Section A.1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Technique de descente et théorèmes d’existence en géométrie algébriques. II. Le théorème d’existence en théorie formelle des modules
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1958-1960__5__369_0"} numdam:SB_1958-1960__5__369_0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §III.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LeinsterYoneda.ps", :title => "The Yoneda Lemma: What's it all about?"} The Yoneda Lemma: What's it all about?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                %em Category Theory in Context. Chapter 2. Universal Properties, Representability, and the Yoneda Lemma
                %a{:href => "https://emilyriehl.github.io/files/context.pdf"} pdf
            %li#RRZ2004
              %p
                Marie La Palme Reyes, Gonzalo E. Reyes, and Houman Zolfaghari,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generic figures and their glueings: A constructive approach to functor categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://reyes-reyes.com/2004/06/01/generic-figures-and-their-glueings-a-constructive-approach-to-functor-categories/"} author page
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "https://marieetgonzalo.files.wordpress.com/2004/06/generic-figures.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Category Theory with examples from basic mathematics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1912.10642"} arXiv
          %p Early Lovász-Type results:
          %ul
            %li#Lovasz1967
              %p
                László Lovász,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operations with structures
                %strong 18
                (1967) 3-4 321-328
            %li#Pultr1973
              %p
                Aleš Pultr.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Isomorphism types of objects in categories determined by numbers of morphisms
                %strong 35
                (1973) 155–160
          %p
            A discussion of the Yoneda lemma from the point of view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vaughan+Pratt"}> Vaughan Pratt
              ,
              %em The Yoneda lemma without category theory: algebra and applications
              (
              %a{:href => "http://boole.stanford.edu/pub/yon.pdf"}> pdf
              ).
          %p
            Discussion of the Yoneda lemma in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+category+theory"} formal category theory
            internal to suitable
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrations and Yoneda’s Lemma in a 2-category
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 420
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0063102"} doi:10.1007/BFb0063102
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elementary cosmoi I
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 420
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/bfb0063103"} doi:10.1007/bfb0063103
          %p
            A treatment of the Yoneda lemma for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} categories internal to an (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Martini"}> Louis Martini
              ,
              %em Yoneda’s lemma for internal higher categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.17141"}> arXiv:2103.17141
              \&amp;rbrack;
